 "puzzleThemes": [],
 "intro": {
  "text": "In the Queen's Gambit Declined Black meets 2.c4 with 2...e6, holding the d5 pawn firmly and opening a diagonal for the dark-squared bishop. The cost is that the light-squared bishop on c8 is blocked in, and finding it a good job is Black's long-term task. In the Orthodox line Black develops with ...Nf6, ...Be7, castles and adds ...Nbd7.",
  "credit": {
   "source": "Wikibooks, Chess Opening Theory/1. d4/1...d5/2. c4/2...e6",
   "url": "https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Chess_Opening_Theory/1._d4/1...d5/2._c4/2...e6",
