     "notes": {
      "text": "3.Nc3 adds pressure on d5 and supports a future e4. 3...Nf6 develops, guards d5 and stops e4, though it allows the pin 4.Bg5. 3...c6 can be met by the sharp 4.e4!? gambit; 3...c5 (Tarrasch) usually accepts an isolated pawn for active pieces; 3...Be7 rules out Bg5.",
